Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Read-only answers for GUIs: why a creature may not attack,
 the defender

Forge's own GUIs mark the creatures that can attack (setWeaklySelectable)
and let the declaration of attackers ignore a click on any other one
(InputAttack.onCardSelected returns false). A GUI that also says why a
creature is not offered - tapped, summoning sick, an effect forbids it -
and which defender a creature tapped now would attack needs Forge's own
answers:

- CombatUtil.attackRefusal(Card, GameEntity): the reason canAttack
  refuses, or null. The checks of canAttack moved unchanged, in the same
  order, into attackRefusal; canAttack is attackRefusal == null. The
  combined basic check is split into single checks in its own order
  (short-circuit order unchanged).
- InputAttack.getCurrentDefender(): the defender a creature declared now
  attacks (the one Forge highlights).
- InputAttack.isSelectablePlayer(Player): whether a click on this player
  would make them the defender (onPlayerSelected's check, moved into
  isDefender, which onCardSelected uses too) and they are not already.

No rule, card or AI behaviour changes: every new method only asks, and
the moved code runs as before.

Written for OpenMana on 2026-09-29.
